    module ImpersonationsOperations
      # Start a support impersonation: a session for `user_id` whose token carries `act.sub` = `staff_user_id`. The instance policy (GET /v1/instance/impersonation_policy) decides the rules: `reason` (max 500 characters) is required unless the policy turns that off, `reason_code` must be one of the policy's codes when it lists any, the session lasts at most the policy's limit (`max_duration_seconds` can only shorten it; never more than 1 hour), and `read_only` (default from the policy) makes the session refuse every change on the Frontend API and puts `ro: true` in its token. When the policy requires approval the call answers 202 with a pending `impersonation_request`; a second staff member decides it with POST /v1/impersonations/requests/{id}/approve or /deny. Optional `require_staff_org_id` and `require_staff_mfa` apply to the staff user (and to the approver). Refused for banned, deleted and impersonation-protected users. Emits `impersonation.started` (and the older `session.impersonation_started`); the user is emailed when the policy says so and sees the session at GET /v1/client/me/staff_access. To export the trail, use GET /v1/audit_logs?action=session.impersonation_started&format=jsonl.
